<p>THE OUTLOOK FOR AUGUST 14-18 CALLS FOR:  temperatures and precipitation to be near normal east and west of the Continental Divide.  Normal temperatures for this period in Montana are highs in the 80s, but 70s in the higher southwest valleys.  Normal lows are in the upper 40s to upper 50s, except in the southwest valleys where the lows are in the lower 40s.</p>
